{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"decoder","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decoding allocates a page table entry for every page of 1024 positions from the first listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position to the end, and a page for each page holding a listed element; positions before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first listed one cost nothing. An end is implausible when that span is more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × count + 64"},{"type":"text","text":" pages, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of vertices (or edges) listed: at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"16 page table entries per listed element (about 2 KB for a vertex, 256 bytes for an edge)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus 64. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"vertexEnd\": 4611686018427387903"},{"type":"text","text":" with no vertices decodes, in O(1), while a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"payload cannot make decoding allocate without limit. A graph that has run more than that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many empty pages past its live elements does not round-trip."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"StableGraphs"}],"title":"init(from:)","extendedModule":"StableGraphs","roleHeading":"Initializer","conformance":{"conformancePr